e Question 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nSam, a 45-year-old introverted scientist, has been struggling for years with social anxiety. Today, he is asked to give a speech in front of numerous respected peers about his recent cutting-edge discovery. But, his wife was the only person who showed up to the speech.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Sam ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Sadness\nB) Disappointment\nC) Anger\nD) Hopeless\nE) Trust\nF) Delight\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Sam feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) He did not have to give a speech to a large group of people, which would have made him very anxious\nB) He wanted more people to show up\nC) He was looking forward to speaking in front of a large gathering\nD) He wanted to overcome his social anxiety by giving the speech","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.00757724180011804,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e8f7d6006945d280af07","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369783118,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:03:03","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"7081ed87db6947a89dab02f87393cabe"}